# Proof and Authority Protocol

Use this rule only when the task involves proof, authority, architecture claims, Gate A/Gate B, live/runtime evidence, or final status reporting.

## Load Discipline

Do not read the full authority stack for routine edits. First select the smallest relevant workspace skill:

- `../../../.agents/skills/gmail-agent-proof-run/SKILL.md` — doctor, replay, bridge, runtime verification.
- `../../../.agents/skills/topinstal-node-topology/SKILL.md` — Node A/B ownership and deployment topology.
- `policy-action-gates` — policy/HITL/execution proof.

Backlog skills (load only if restored): `release-gate-proof-pack`, `daszek-v3-projection-audit`, `case-context-memory-pack`.

Read deeper docs only when claims require them, not by default.

## Proof Rules

- Local files are not live proof.
- Static repo graph is not runtime proof.
- MCP output is not Gate B proof.
- Daszek fixture success is not WordPress/operator proof.
- Default: local Docker only; VPS/prod requires explicit operator scope.
- Separate: implemented / tested locally / stack smoke / operator verified / not proven.
- Use labels from workspace `92-proof-gate-discipline.mdc`.

## Topology and Pack Truth

Multi-repo workspace: identify owning nested Git repo and physical node before claims. Node A and Node B communicate via REST bridge, not shared filesystem.

## Root Cause Discipline

Hold at least two hypotheses until one is falsified with file-path, command, log, or external evidence. If graph MCP is stale, fall back to runbooks and source reads.

## Durable State

After substantive proof/handover, update `../../../knowledge/memory/LAST_SESSION.md` only when operator instructs per `../../../knowledge/SESSION_MEMORY_POLICY.md`. Do not use `memory-bank/`.
